@startuml fig02_component
!include theme.iuml
title Figure 2 — Component View: Control Plane, Data Path, and the Shared-Policy Boundary

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 42

package "Measurement harness — Week-1 deliverable (F-16 – F-20)" #FFFCF5 {
  [gen_trace.py\ndeterministic, offline] as GEN
  artifact "trace.jsonl + run_manifest.json\nconfig hash · seed · code revision" as TRACE
  [replay.py\nopen-loop · no runtime RNG] as REP
}

package "Client tier" {
  [Thin Client] as CLIENT
}

package "Control plane — centralised scheduler (F-12)" {
  [Admission Filter\nF-13 / F-14] as ADM
  [Cost Model\nF-6 / F-7] as CM
  [Capability View\n+ Staleness Injector · F-8] as CAP
  [Batch-Aware Router\nF-4 / F-5] as BAR
  [Dispatch Policy\nfive policies, one interface · F-1 / F-2] as POL
  [Heartbeat Collector\nF-10] as HB
  [Decision Logger\nF-3] as DLOG
}

package "Worker tier — one full replica per node" {
  [Worker Wrapper\nF-9] as WW
  [llama.cpp engine · GGUF] as LCPP <<reused>>
}

package "Simulation (F-21 – F-24)" #FFFCF5 {
  [Service-Time Model\nfitted + stochastic · F-22] as STM
  [Discrete-Event Simulator] as DES
}

package "Records and analysis (F-18 – F-20, F-23)" #FFFCF5 {
  database "per-process JSONL" as LOGS
  [Record Joiner\njoin on req_id] as JOIN
  [Validator\np50 / p95 tolerance] as VAL
  [Figure Scripts] as FIG
}

GEN -down-> TRACE
TRACE -down-> REP
REP -down-> CLIENT : release at\nscheduled offset
CLIENT -down-> ADM : **Submit**\ngRPC · req_id in metadata
ADM -down-> CAP
CM -right-> CAP
CAP -down-> POL
BAR -right-> POL
HB -up-> CAP
POL -right-> DLOG
POL -down-> WW : **Dispatch**\ngRPC
WW -up-> HB : **Heartbeat**\ngRPC stream
WW -down-> LCPP
WW -[#B45309]up-> CLIENT : **full response**\nworker to client, direct · F-11

TRACE -right-> DES : same trace replayed\nacross the boundary (F-17)
POL .[#B45309].> DES : **the same policy objects**\nnot a reimplementation (F-21)
STM -down-> DES

DLOG -down-> LOGS
WW -right-> LOGS
CLIENT -right-> LOGS
DES -down-> LOGS
LOGS -right-> JOIN
JOIN -down-> VAL
JOIN -down-> FIG

note right of POL
  RoundRobin · JSQ · StaticWeighted · WJSQ · Threshold(T)
  Selected by one configuration value, with no code
  change between runs.
end note

note bottom of WW
  One runtime on every node, GPU and CPU alike (F-9), so engine-internal
  batching is **one mechanism rather than two** and R is a property of
  hardware and configuration alone. Engine internals are never modified:
  batching is owned inside the engine (F-5) and the scheduler influences
  batch composition only by choosing where to route (F-4).
end note

legend right
  <color:#BFD6D1>███</color>  system under study
  <color:#EBC98F>███</color>  instrumentation
  <color:#C9C9C2>███</color>  reused third-party runtime
endlegend
@enduml
